      ":question/problem": "Find $(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}$, where $t>-3$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln{\\left(t + 3 \\right)} \\\\ \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ 2 \\sqrt{t + 3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}e^{3 t} \\\\ \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{t + 3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the **sum and constant multiple rules**:\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)+2\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t + 3} \\\\ - 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t + 3}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}3 e^{3 t} \\\\ 3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nScale every component by its constant multiplier:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{t + 3} \\\\ - 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t + 3}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ 2\\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{3 t} \\\\ 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding components and combine like terms:\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{f}(t)+2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{\\prime}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{3 t} + \\frac{2}{t + 3} \\\\ - 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}} + \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t + 3}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nKeep the displayed inner arguments when applying the scalar derivative rules; any nonunit inner derivative multiplies its component.",
